WEBVTT

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.520
Minions, assemble!

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.880
Okay. Okay.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.760
Hey!

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.800
Looking good, Kevin!
How is the family? Good?

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.040
All right.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.000
That's my Billy boy!
What up, Larry?

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.960
Hello, everybody!

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.840
Yeah, all right!

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.160
Simmer down. Simmer down!

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.040
Thank you, okay.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.880
Now, I realise that you guys
probably heard

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.640
about this other villain
who stole the pyramids.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.960
Apparently, it's a big deal.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.320
People are calling it
the crime of the century and stuff
like that.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.400
But am I upset? No, I am not!

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.200
A little,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.040
but we have had
a pretty good year ourselves,

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.880
and you guys
are all right in my book.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.160
No, no raises!

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.280
You're not going to get any raises.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.680
What did we do?

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:07.520
Well, we stole the Times Square
JumboTron!

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.160
Nice!

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:12.720
That's how I roll.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.640
Yeah, you all like watching
football on that, huh?

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.760
But that's not all.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.000
We stole the Statue of Liberty,

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.880
the small one from Las Vegas.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.840
And I won't even mention
the Eiffel Tower! Also Vegas.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.600
Okay, I wasn't going to tell you
about this yet,

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.160
but I have been working
on something very big!

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.240
Something that will blow this
pyramid thing out of the water!

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.000
And thanks to the efforts
of my good friend Dr Nefario...

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.760
Thank you!

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.080
There he is.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.560
He's styling.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.360
Now, we have located a shrink ray

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.880
in a secret lab,
and once we take this shrink ray,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.240
we will have the capability

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:09.120
to pull off the true crime
of the century.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.200
We are going to steal...

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.320
Wait, wait! I haven't told you
what it is yet.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.080
Hey.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.200
Dave, listen up, please.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.880
Next, we are going to steal,

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.240
pause for effect,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.080
the moon!

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.880
And once the moon is mine,

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.520
the world will give me
whatever I want to get it back!

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.720
And I will be the greatest villain
of all time!

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.640
That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.240
Yes?

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.880
Hello, Gru?
I've been crunching some numbers,

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.040
and I really don't see how we can
afford this.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.800
It can't be done.
I'm not a miracle worker.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.800
Hey, chillax.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.360
I'll just get another loan
from the bank. They love me!

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.040
Edith, stop it!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.120
What? I'm just walking.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.440
- Hi, Miss Hattie. We're back.
- Hi, Miss Hattie. We're back.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.640
Hello, girls!

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:57.440
Anybody come to adopt us
while we were out?

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.240
Let me think.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:01.760
No!

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.800
Edith! What did you put on my desk?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.800
A mud pie.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.280
You're never gonna get adopted,
Edith. You know that, don't you?

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.560
- Yeah, I know.
- Good.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:20.080
So, how did it go, girls?
Did we meet our quotas?

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.160
Sort of.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.320
We sold 43 mini-mints, 30 choco-
swirlies, and 18 coco-nutties.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.240
Okay.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.320
Well, you say that like it's
a great sale day.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.480
Look at my face!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.680
Do you still think it's a great
sale day?

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.480
Eighteen coco-nutties.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.360
I think we can do a little better
than that, don't you?

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.160
Yeah.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.720
We wouldn't want to spend
the weekend in the Box of Shame,

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:53.280
would we? No.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:54.960
- No, Miss Hattie.
- No, Miss Hattie.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.600
Okay, good. Off you go.
Go clean something of mine.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.760
- Hi, Penny.
- Hi, Penny.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:02.960
Hi, guys.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:10.800
Hello, Mom. Sorry,
I meant to call, but...

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.280
I just wanted to congratulate you
on stealing the pyramid.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.640
That was you, wasn't it?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.360
Or was it a villain
who's actually successful?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:24.080
Just so you know, Mom,
I am about to do something

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.800
that's very, very big,
very important.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.840
When you hear about it,
you're going to be very proud.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.360
Good luck with that.
Okay, I'm out of here.

